{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1563104-vampire-lore-galore","id":1563104,"title":"Vampire Lore Galore","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-08-14T12:12:13-07:00","id":1563104,"title":"Vampire Lore Galore","content":"This is not about folklore, legends or literature, although it is influenced by those.<br /> <br /> My goal here is to lump in one place ideas for vampires and their traits, for use in any game. Everyone is welcome to give ideas that can be applied to make for more interesting monsters as PCs or foes.<br /> <br /> Folklore is a great place to look for inspiration, but it must be clear first that you won't find any about what we know as vampires. The creature proper, an intelligent undead that drink blood to extend their lives for eternity, stalking the night with passion and socially apt, is a 19th century literary creation.<br /> <br /> When looking for the actual old lore, a creature is a vampire if it meets <i>any</i> of the following:<br /> <br /> 1. It feeds on blood, including animal blood.<br /> <br /> 2. It is an animated corpse, or Revenant.<br /> <br /> 3. It steals the vitality of the living<br /> <br /> How to implement the lore in your game is up to you, but I can give some ideas based on the type of lore. You can always use it to make new NPCs, but I think giving some new takes to PCs is more interesting.<br /> <br /> Next I'll post what I made so far regarding the means to destroy a vampire. Some are direct from folklore from all around the word, some adapted from wards and protective charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T12:24:56-07:00","id":1563106,"title":"","content":"On destroying vampires<br /> <br /> The following have been used to ward or finish undead in many places. You can port them to a game in two main ways: they may add to the weaknesses of the creature, giving hunters an edge, or they can substitute, rendering previous methods ineffective.<br /> <br /> For PCs, or if you fear a NPC will be too tough, you can balance the later with nonlethal means to disable the vampire for a time. Masquerade and Requiem both have this in place as Torpor, so as long as the difficulty to beat a Kindred remains the same, how to destroy them ceases to be a balance factor. <hr /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T13:47:50-07:00","id":1563107,"title":"","content":"How about the Tziscme feeling a need to be complusive counters to play into their need for total control of the environment and inhuman seeming nature?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T20:29:57-07:00","id":1563111,"title":"","content":"Thorough ritual -&gt; you have to stake, then behead, then burn, possibly with blessed items all the time while chanting hymns.<br /> <br /> Overkill -&gt; dump the vampire in an active volcano. Be sure they hit the lava rather than landing in a nook.<br /> <br /> Disable the body -&gt; you can remove the head and place it between their legs to make lifting structurally demanding, or stuff the mouth with pebbles so it can't bite, or puncture the heart to stop pumping.<br /> <br /> Farming scythe -&gt; use a farming scythe to take the heart or head out. It's way easier if a scythe was positioned in the corpse for this beforehand, as it isn't a weapon.<br /> <br /> Read their True Names -&gt; the creature has a list of names with power over it. They must be read in order before a command or prayer.<br /> <br /> Stuff with Apotropaics -&gt; sacred bread, prayer beads, garlic, anything considered to ward evil. Stuffing the nose, mouth or both is standard.<br /> <br /> Pour wine -&gt; must be done during the day, on the dead corpse. Sometimes has to be blessed or has to be a particular type of wine. May be necessary to marinate. In areas where funeral cannibalism is practiced, may be necessary to eat, in accordance with proper rites.<br /> <br /> Starvation -&gt; keep the vampire bound but alert during the night, denying it any blood, until they turn into a decayed corpse.<br /> <br /> Hide the target -&gt; a vampire that always feeds from the same spot in the body, like neck or the toes, will die in shock if they track a suitable prey, but can't find the target.<br /> <br /> Trapped house -&gt; in the Easter Sunday undead gather in the church with the living. If a cross made of pig bones is placed over the entrance of the church in this day, they won't be able to leave. Instead, upon trying they'll stop in the threshold and at this moment alone they can be killed.<br /> <br /> Bloodied coin -&gt; follow the vampire to the woods and wait for it to vomit the blood and go away. Soak a silver coin in the blood, then wrap it in a cloth. If the ritual alone doesn't kill the vampire, they'll die upon seeing the talisman. If still don't work they'll avoid you anyway, for a hit of the talisman will do them for good.<br /> <br /> Pierce the heart with -&gt; if just piercing the heart isn't enough, try with specific objects and/or materials. Iron nails, iron stakes, stakes of yew or other particular tree. Sometimes you pierce the neck, stomach or other organ.<br /> <br /> Scatter the ashes -&gt; cremation is necessary, the corpse won't burn easily and must burn as completely as possible. The more you can scatter the ashes, the better.<br /> <br /> Special burial -&gt; kill it with a sword made of yew, then bury the corpse upside down.<br /> <br /> Blessed fire -&gt; to burn the vampire, the fire must start from wood pieces just taken out of a church.<br /> <br /> Disease -&gt; the vampire must contract a terrible disease like Cholera, Typhoid, Tuberculosis, the Plague or something.<br /> <br /> Specific hunter -&gt; only people born in Saturday can kill the vampire.<br /> <br /> Pinned with iron -&gt; a stake is used, but instead of targeting the heart, it must trespass the body and fix the vampire in place.<br /> <br /> Mashed garlic -&gt; mash garlic and add wine. Mix. Plaster the result in the frames of door and windows at the vampire's house.<br /> <br /> Day burning -&gt; stalk the grave of the vampire until a night when they come to pass the day. Wait until the sun is high enough and take the vampire out of the earth. It will awaken and will probably fight, but you have to conduct the rest while it resists, you can't bind it. Conduct a full prayer of Exorcism while burning the vampire.<br /> <br /> Twin ward -&gt; the vampire will be vulnerable to death if two twin brothers get two twin oxen and plow around the village or area where the monster hunts.<br /> <br /> Beneath a bier -&gt; during the wake of the person who is or may become a vampire, one attendee must crawl beneath the bier with an egg and an iron nail. Break the egg, then drive the nail through the yolk and into the floor. If the house where it happens belongs to the deceased, the curse is no more.<br /> <br /> In the cemetery -&gt; two or three elderly women must attend the cemetery the evening after the funeral and stick five hawthorne pegs or old knives into the grave: one at the position of the deceased's chest, and the other four at the positions of their arms and legs. The pegs can be new, but must be made by hand. The knives must be older than the transformation.<br /> <br /> Backward hunting -&gt; a bait wait at the foot of a hill with a lit candle in one hand and a turtle in the other, until the vampire starts to stalk them. Then the bait must start to run backwards up the hill, and as long as they do so, the candle is lit and the turtle alive, the vampire won't be able to touch them. After the vampire returns to their resting place, surround it with a red woolen thread, ignite the thread, and wait until it was burnt up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T21:58:31-07:00","id":1563112,"title":"","content":"Salt and fish -&gt; when the vampire is sneaking around your house, shout for it to hear &quot;Come tomorrow, and I will give you some salt.&quot; The vampire must go for the night. Leave the salt in the next night and wait for the creature to take it, then shout &quot;Go, pal, get some fish, and come back.\u201d The vampire will get weaker every night until they bring salted fish, though they won't die of this weakness. The salted fish will ward this vampire, and a person that eats every bite of the fish will be able to destroy the vampire.<br /> <br /> Watchful twins -&gt; a twin brother and sister born on a Saturday who wore their clothes inside out can see a vampire no matter what trick or power it uses. The vampire can be destroyed by them or with their guidance as long as both are watching it. The vampire will know they're being observed, though, and will try to escape.<br /> <br /> Babosa's drool -&gt; hung aloe vera backwards behind a door the vampire uses. If the creature pass through the door, the gel in the plant will become like a burning poison to this vampire. If the vampire takes the blood of someone inside the house, they'll suck only aloe vera gel instead, which won't be poisonous if they didn't pass through the guarded door, but will be disgusting nonetheless, as I unfortunately can attest.<br /> <br /> Burn the heart -&gt; the organ must be extracted whole first, without any wound or blemish, or it will shriver and the vampire will be invulnerable until a new heart grows. The removed heart must be burn to ashes away from the vampire.<br /> <br /> Catch by thorns -&gt; a vampire avoid areas with living plants with big thorns, as their wounds are deep and painful, albeit normal. Thorns that sipped the blood of the monster can kill it later, but the first wound must come from the living plant. Those undead with exposed entrails are particularly fearful of such plants.<br /> <br /> Hair in the mouth -&gt; fill their mouth with their own hair. Some need to be cut first, others need to be still attached, but is always one or the other.<br /> <br /> For careful burial -&gt; fill the mouth of the corpse with glass beads, put an egg under each armpit and needles in the palms. Bury carefully, for the beads, eggs and needles must all remain in place until the next sunrise.<br /> <br /> Paper seal -&gt; use a slip of special paper from a shrine. Write in it the vampire's name, date of birth, the names of the families of their father and mother, and grandfather and grandmother, and any lord or god they held allegiance to. If everything is correct, the vampire will be under spell and follow you quietly, though they'll be taken by rigor mortis. You must then conduct the vampire to their birthplace by foot and bury them in the local cemetery.<br /> <br /> Red beer -&gt; if a vampire mistake red beer for blood, the beer will make them drunk as it would a living person (which may require a lot of beer). The drunk vampire is still invulnerable, but is calm and pliable if not provoked. If you can convince the creature to change their ways during this time, they'll hold to their word and become something else, ceasing to be a vampire.<br /> <br /> Witnessed by a woman -&gt; when the vampire target a man for a great evil or to make him into a servant, and the vampire moves in to live with the man or call the man and his family, at least one woman in the house will be made able to pierce any disguise or deception. If this woman chooses to tell the man, and the man is loyal enough to trust her beyond the spells of the vampire, only then this man will be capable at killing the vampire. If the man is abusive against the woman in question and the woman chooses to flee, the vampire will never be able to harm her or those she took with her, or find them with ill intent, but the life of the man will be forfeited.<br /> <br /> Divorce -&gt; the vampire cannot touch divorce papers, and cannot approach someone who recite a formal offering of divorce. If the person is officially married to the vampire and the papers are real, serving them will paralyze the vampire, and touching them to the vampire will destroy the creature.<br /> <br /> Chains -&gt; the vampire can be destroyed by the removal of the head, but their neck can't be cut unless the vampire is in iron chains with seven locks.<br /> <br /> Incantation Bowl -&gt; an artisan with the right technique must make a bowl for this particular vampire, and inside inscribe the ritual and the incantations to be used, in a spiral and in the proper alphabet. A drawing of the vampire rest in the center, and the vampire must see it when the time comes.<br /> <br /> At least seven living people not under the spell of the vampire must wear clothes made with fiber of fig and stay with the vampire for days and nights, sleeping in the same room. The more and/or the merrier, so much faster will the vampire die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T12:01:51-07:00","id":1563260,"title":"","content":"If we're using folk lore, there's a bunch of different ways one can become a vampire that don't involve being embraced.<br /> <br /> Those who have <b>blue eyes</b> and <b>red hair</b> are said to become vampires upon death.<br /> <br /> The seventh son born of seven sons will likewise return as a vampire.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are said to become vampires after death, if their bodies are not properly disposed of.<br /> <br /> Suicide victims can become vampires, as can those who were denied proper burial rites.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------<br /> <br /> Also, vampires originally did not have an aversion to sunlight. That didn't really become a popular thing until Count Orlock came along, and it was later co-opted by Dracula.<br /> <br /> It was also believed vampires had the ability to become immaterial and phase through solid obstacles. Which explains how they were able to rise from their graves each night, without disturbing the earth around it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T12:02:48-07:00","id":1563261,"title":"","content":"Then I am cursed with undeath as I have blue eyes \ud83d\udc41\ufe0f \ud83d\udc40.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T12:12:35-07:00","id":1563263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1563104-vampire-lore-galore?p=1563261#post1563261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then I am cursed with undeath as I have blue eyes \ud83d\udc41\ufe0f \ud83d\udc40.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the hair?<br /> <br /> It has to be a blue eyes and red hair combo!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T13:09:32-07:00","id":1563264,"title":"","content":"I have greying light brown hair that was a shade or two away from being blonde.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T17:05:01-07:00","id":1563272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1563104-vampire-lore-galore?p=1563264#post1563264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have greying light brown hair that was a shade or two away from being blonde.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you're safe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T23:38:02-07:00","id":1563274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1563104-vampire-lore-galore?p=1563260#post1563260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're using folk lore, there's a bunch of different ways one can become a vampire that don't involve being embraced.<br /> <br /> Those who have <b>blue eyes</b> and <b>red hair</b> are said to become vampires upon death.<br /> <br /> The seventh son born of seven sons will likewise return as a vampire.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are said to become vampires after death, if their bodies are not properly disposed of.<br /> <br /> Suicide victims can become vampires, as can those who were denied proper burial rites.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------<br /> <br /> Also, vampires originally did not have an aversion to sunlight. That didn't really become a popular thing until Count Orlock came along, and it was later co-opted by Dracula.<br /> <br /> It was also believed vampires had the ability to become immaterial and phase through solid obstacles. Which explains how they were able to rise from their graves each night, without disturbing the earth around it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget that you can become a vampire if a wolf or a vampire jumps over your body, or if certain birds fly over your corpse.<br /> <br /> But most vampires are just born vampires, be them spirits or living monsters. You can also become a vampire still alive, either on purpose or cursed with hunger for blood.<br /> <br /> The sun is a curious thing. From the first Vampyre, Lord Ruthven, until Count Orlok, we saw pass more than a hundred years. Before that we had at most vampires that slept during the day, but nothing about being harmed by the sun. Carmilla just didn't like it, and Dracula lost a few powers that may have been sorcery.<br /> <br /> Also, he's probably not a reference to Vlad III the Impaler. Stoker's diary in the end has no sign that the author ever heard about Vlad at all, he just found out that Dracula was a nickname in the overall region and thought it was cool. The similarity is, indeed, a coincidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-06T18:20:48-07:00","id":1563875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1563104-vampire-lore-galore?p=1563274#post1563274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, he's probably not a reference to Vlad III the Impaler. Stoker's diary in the end has no sign that the author ever heard about Vlad at all, he just found out that Dracula was a nickname in the overall region and thought it was cool. The similarity is, indeed, a coincidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of, Dracula wasn't killed by a wooden steak in the original story. They stabbed him with a silver knife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-06T21:42:55-07:00","id":1563881,"title":"","content":"Indeed in the novel by Bram Stoker he never has Count Dracula ever refer himself as Vlad The Impaler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-06T22:45:16-07:00","id":1563882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1563104-vampire-lore-galore?p=1563875#post1563875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of, Dracula wasn't killed by a wooden steak in the original story. They stabbed him with a silver knife.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a little more complicated.<br /> <br /> To defeat Dracula they research every possible thing that empowers him and cut him off of the sources.<br /> <br /> First, and that takes a lot of the story, they work to undo his preparations to make England safe. They overtake or destroy havens, track and use mystic rituals to sabotage the portions of earth he brought from Transylvania. They don't even consider trying to take him feasible until they render England completely unlivable for him.<br /> <br /> Even then, that's only part 1, and part 2 must happen in the limited window of his escape. Van Helsing and Mina go ahead of everyone because they have to handle the more mystical challenges of the hunt: fucking overtake the castle, destroy all the Brides and cleanse his main sleeping chamber.<br /> <br /> Weakening Dracula's seat of power was viable only because he literally didn't left any defense whatsoever, but his decision is understandable, his Brides are powerhouses in their own right. To kill them in an otherwise empty castle Van Helsing still needed a whole day as he had to ritually stake, behead and stuff them with garlic in their Day Sleep, while Mina regularly brought him out of the trance induced by their powers.<br /> <br /> Let this set in: killing Lucy earlier in the novel is already way harder than the average vampire killing in other stories, yet Lucy is actually the easier one. An actual full fledged Bride would have turned her wannabe killers into servants just from trying.<br /> <br /> Mina is paramount in their success. While she is not like in the League Extraordinary movie, being magically bound to Dracula does give her a number of powers that proved necessary. It's her power that lets them find all his protection preparations back in England, spy on his travel back to Transylvania, and several other tricks that are risky to try, but absolutely necessary. Against the Brides in particular it wouldn't have been possible to either locate, live through the night or act against them at all.<br /> <br /> Part 3 is to intercept the Count during the day, in the castle grounds, but only after the other parts are complete. They had to ambush his servants, fight for the cask, and actually the execution has two parts, the silver Bowie Knife to the heart and a blessed kukri to the throat with the sun light touching the Count, all three at the same time.<br /> <br /> As par of the course for the Gothic tradition, it is unclear what exactly in the whole debacle did the deed, so it's left in the air if anything beyond the knife to the heart was necessary. But Van Helsing did believe it was everything, and a single piece out of place would left the Undead invulnerable (fun to remind, but in this book Undead isn't a common term, it is one of Dracula's main epithets specifically).<br /> <br /> Just to remember that while he's not Varney (who dies by voluntarily jumping in a volcano), Dracula is absurdly hard to kill. And if none of the usual methods destroy him, in a sense that is because the requires all of them, directly or by proxy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-07T03:35:04-07:00","id":1563887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1563104-vampire-lore-galore?p=1563882#post1563882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As par of the course for the Gothic tradition, it is unclear what exactly in the whole debacle did the deed, so it's left in the air if anything beyond the knife to the heart was necessary. But Van Helsing did believe it was everything, and a single piece out of place would left the Undead invulnerable (fun to remind, but in this book Undead isn't a common term, it is one of Dracula's main epithets specifically).<br /> <br /> Just to remember that while he's not Varney (who dies by voluntarily jumping in a volcano), Dracula is absurdly hard to kill. And if none of the usual methods destroy him, in a sense that is because the requires all of them, directly or by proxy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny that some mythology states you have to slay the vampire while they're in their coffin. Because I've also heard conflicting mythology state that if you place the vampire's ashes back inside their coffin, they will regenerate again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-09T19:29:35-07:00","id":1563946,"title":"","content":"The best way to slay a vampire is to launch them towards a black-hole; it will take millions of years to get there, but, they got the time. <br /> <br /> And I can see, like Blood-bathers, being mistake for vampires in a WoD game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-10T11:07:54-07:00","id":1563955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1563104-vampire-lore-galore?p=1563946#post1563946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best way to slay a vampire is to launch them towards a black-hole; it will take millions of years to get there, but, they got the time.<br /> <br /> And I can see, like Blood-bathers, being mistake for vampires in a WoD game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure they'd be nuked by unfiltered solar radiation, long before they ever reached a black hole.<br /> <br /> Also, if the vampire has the power of magical flight, they could just change course back towards earth... assuming they didn't burn up on reentry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-10T14:22:20-07:00","id":1563961,"title":"","content":"From a folklore standpoint blood bathers are vampires. It is the distinction that's arbitrary, not the recognition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-10T17:08:38-07:00","id":1563966,"title":"","content":"That reminds of the novel series from the 1990s called Family Dracul and the second book or was it the 3rd book had The Blood Countess Bathorny and she was classified as a vampire despite being able to walk into the sun and no real fears of religious objects like her cousin Vlad Dracul did. <br /> <br /> That was a good series when I read it as a young adult, I wonder if if I would like it now as a much older adult?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-10T19:14:30-07:00","id":1563968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1563104-vampire-lore-galore?p=1563955#post1563955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty sure they'd be nuked by unfiltered solar radiation, long before they ever reached a black hole.<br /> <br /> Also, if the vampire has the power of magical flight, they could just change course back towards earth... assuming they didn't burn up on reentry.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Like a vampire would know astrogation. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-10T19:53:44-07:00","id":1563970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1563104-vampire-lore-galore?p=1563966#post1563966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That reminds of the novel series from the 1990s called Family Dracul and the second book or was it the 3rd book had The Blood Countess Bathorny and she was classified as a vampire despite being able to walk into the sun and no real fears of religious objects like her cousin Vlad Dracul did.<br /> <br /> That was a good series when I read it as a young adult, I wonder if if I would like it now as a much older adult?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bathory is a regular in stories about vampires, it's weird for a setting with vamps to not have her as one. Yet we have plenty testimony that she didn't mind the sun or holy objects.<br /> <br /> Carmilla, who's likely to have been based on her, didn't either. She preferred the night, but suffered no ill effect from any of those besides waking up late during the day, but she still wake up at day. She avoided church service, but that was the extent of it and wasn't totally uncommon at the time, she has no problem with most religious iconography.<br /> <br /> Her destruction in the book is the basis for the Brides of Dracula: lots of blessings, stake, behead, burn thoroughly. Has religious tones all over, but it's too extreme for her to fear such objects in a regular day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-11-04T11:19:34-08:00","id":1565133,"title":"","content":"<b>Yet another piece of lore:</b> the reason why vampires are afraid of running water, isn't because it burns like acid, but because if the vampire is destroyed while they are in physical contact with it, their souls will become trapped inside the water for eternity.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, you can become a vampire if they bite you six times in a single night.<br /> <br /> Then there's the lore about how they have OCD when it comes to counting. If you find yourself being chased by a vampire, spill a bag of grain on the ground and run. The vampire will be compelled to stop and count every single piece, even as the sun is rising.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}